            // `NonNull::new` note in `total_no_panic_call_summary`), so std's own SAFE
            // constructor performs exactly this check. The extractor's `ptr_to_nonnull` leg admits such casts today
            // and charges NOTHING, which is why R105's probe found the non-null premise
            // simply unknown rather than established.
            //
            // Emit `src != 0` and ASSERT it — unannotated, so it stays REFUTABLE (the
            // R87 `UncheckedBinaryOp` discipline: never discard the flag). The assert
            // joins the function's whole-function panic-freedom aggregate; unproved,
            // that row publishes `runtime_checked`, which the default (strict) policy
            // passes and `-Ztrust-policy=certify` refuses (docs/KNOWN_HAZARDS.md, "a
            // whole-function panic-freedom row that reads `runtime_checked`"), although
